WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.256 --> 00:00:02.834
-You know my next guest
from his breakout role

00:00:02.834 --> 00:00:04.133
in "Stranger Things."

00:00:04.133 --> 00:00:06.267
Now he's starring
alongside Idris Elba

00:00:06.267 --> 00:00:08.367
in the new movie
"Concrete Cowboy,"

00:00:08.367 --> 00:00:10.267
which is streaming now
on Netflix.

00:00:10.267 --> 00:00:12.300
Here is Caleb McLaughlin!

00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:13.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:13.634 --> 00:00:15.734
Yeah, that's what
I'm talking about!

00:00:15.734 --> 00:00:18.634
That's my man.
How are you, bud?

00:00:18.634 --> 00:00:20.067
-I'm good. How are you doing?

00:00:20.067 --> 00:00:21.467
-I'm doing great. Welcome back.

00:00:21.467 --> 00:00:22.801
Thank you so much
for doing the show.

00:00:22.801 --> 00:00:24.133
I appreciate it.

00:00:24.133 --> 00:00:26.801
I want to get into your movie.
I thought it was so good.

00:00:26.801 --> 00:00:30.801
And I was looking through
some IMDB stuff.

00:00:30.801 --> 00:00:32.601
I was looking through
just Internet stuff,

00:00:32.601 --> 00:00:35.934
rumors about you, and I wanted
to ask you this question.

00:00:35.934 --> 00:00:37.234
There's a rumor out there

00:00:37.234 --> 00:00:40.167
that you're going to
release some music?

00:00:40.167 --> 00:00:42.167
-Yeah, yeah, I am.

00:00:42.167 --> 00:00:46.968
I'm excited. I'm trying to drop
something this year.

00:00:46.968 --> 00:00:49.567
-What is your music like?
What's the album gonna be like?

00:00:49.567 --> 00:00:51.300
-Man, I mean,

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:54.133
I've been working with this
producer, Rashad, on music.

00:00:54.133 --> 00:00:57.534
He's been helping me cultivate
my sound and what I like.

00:00:57.534 --> 00:01:01.501
It's like neo soul, R&amp;B,
a lot of Afrobeats.

00:01:01.501 --> 00:01:03.133
It's a whole bunch of stuff,
man.

00:01:03.133 --> 00:01:04.300
-That's so exciting.

00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:05.634
-You know what's funny?

00:01:05.634 --> 00:01:07.834
A lot of people,
when they ask me

00:01:07.834 --> 00:01:09.734
do I do music,
they think I'm a rapper.

00:01:09.734 --> 00:01:12.067
And I tell them yeah
and then I make up a name.

00:01:12.067 --> 00:01:13.701
And I'm like,
"Yeah, my name is Centric."

00:01:13.701 --> 00:01:15.701
They're like, "What?
That's crazy."

00:01:15.701 --> 00:01:17.267
-Centric?
-But I'm like, "Nah."

00:01:17.267 --> 00:01:19.601
Centric, yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:19.601 --> 00:01:21.634
But it's a total lie.
I'm not a rapper.

00:01:21.634 --> 00:01:23.868
I can't rap for my life.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:23.868 --> 00:01:25.901
-But why not? Yeah, do it. Yeah.

00:01:25.901 --> 00:01:29.200
We had your pal,
Gaten Matarazzo, on the show.

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:30.934
Gosh, was it two days ago?

00:01:30.934 --> 00:01:33.767
And I was asking about
"Stranger Things" obviously.

00:01:33.767 --> 00:01:37.267
And he said that all he knows
about this season

00:01:37.267 --> 00:01:40.067
is that it's the scariest season
by far.

00:01:40.067 --> 00:01:42.033
-I mean, he's right.

00:01:42.033 --> 00:01:44.934
I feel like every season
gets scarier and more gritty.

00:01:44.934 --> 00:01:47.400
-Yeah.
-He's very true, yeah.

00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:49.200
-Yeah. But this one picks up.

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:54.033
So, I mean, obviously everyone
is growing up and getting older.

00:01:54.033 --> 00:01:56.200
Do you know how
you're gonna handle this?

00:01:56.200 --> 00:01:57.834
What age are you
gonna be in this?

00:01:57.834 --> 00:02:00.467
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, I know everyone is like,

00:02:00.467 --> 00:02:02.601
"Wow, you look so old
and your voice is deep.

00:02:02.601 --> 00:02:03.868
You got a beard."

00:02:03.868 --> 00:02:05.901
I'm like, "Yeah, it's just
facial hair. Don't worry.

00:02:05.901 --> 00:02:07.901
I've always played young
my whole life.

00:02:07.901 --> 00:02:11.868
Like, people don't realize
in Season 1, I played 14.

00:02:11.868 --> 00:02:14.033
And I was supposed to play
like an 11-year-old.

00:02:14.033 --> 00:02:15.100
So I'm used to it.

00:02:15.100 --> 00:02:18.000
-Yeah, and you're 54 years old.

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:22.033
[ Laughter ]

00:02:22.033 --> 00:02:23.734
-I'm 54.
-That's the magic, yeah.

00:02:23.734 --> 00:02:26.934
I mean, you're still young.
Come on. Are you kidding me?

00:02:26.934 --> 00:02:29.334
Alright, so, yeah. So you'll
figure out some way to do it.

00:02:29.334 --> 00:02:31.901
I want to talk about your movie
"Concrete Cowboy."

00:02:31.901 --> 00:02:33.667
It started streaming last week.

00:02:33.667 --> 00:02:35.934
And guess what.
Number-one movie on Netflix.

00:02:35.934 --> 00:02:37.701
Not too bad.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:37.701 --> 00:02:40.868
-Nah, it's not too bad at all.
It's great. Blessings.

00:02:40.868 --> 00:02:43.300
-I didn't know anything
about this story,

00:02:43.300 --> 00:02:44.767
and I thought
it was fascinating.

00:02:44.767 --> 00:02:47.501
It's a real community
in Philadelphia, right?

00:02:47.501 --> 00:02:49.534
[ Man whoos ]
-Yep, yep, yep, yep.

00:02:49.534 --> 00:02:51.367
[ Laughter ]
-That wasn't even a whoo.

00:02:51.367 --> 00:02:52.667
What?
That sounded like an animal.

00:02:52.667 --> 00:02:54.434
[ Laughter ]

00:02:54.434 --> 00:02:56.400
That sounded like a dog got hit
by a car.

00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:57.601
It was like...
[ Yelps ]

00:02:57.601 --> 00:03:00.734
[ Laughter ]

00:03:00.734 --> 00:03:02.234
Do you guys know about this?

00:03:02.234 --> 00:03:04.767
It's the Fletcher Street
Urban Riding Club.

00:03:04.767 --> 00:03:06.300
-Yeah, Fletcher Street.
-Yep.

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:07.734
-The Roots know about this.

00:03:07.734 --> 00:03:10.434
-Yep. Okay, got you, got you.
-Yeah, they're from Philly.

00:03:10.434 --> 00:03:11.934
-I didn't know
anything about it.

00:03:11.934 --> 00:03:16.133
-Yeah. Can you set up the movie
for anyone who hasn't seen it?

00:03:16.133 --> 00:03:17.601
-Oh, yeah, of course.

00:03:17.601 --> 00:03:19.133
Well, as you already know,

00:03:19.133 --> 00:03:21.834
it's taking place in Fletcher
Street in North Philadelphia.

00:03:21.834 --> 00:03:24.200
It's taking place --

00:03:24.200 --> 00:03:27.567
Well, it's seen through the
character, my character, Cole.

00:03:27.567 --> 00:03:28.934
And he's sent to live with

00:03:28.934 --> 00:03:30.834
his estranged father
in Philadelphia.

00:03:30.834 --> 00:03:32.434
In his time down there,

00:03:32.434 --> 00:03:34.701
he learns about
the urban cowboy culture.

00:03:34.701 --> 00:03:36.901
-Yeah, and it's a real thing.

00:03:36.901 --> 00:03:40.000
And it's basically
saying to people,

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:41.367
"Hey, this is
another alternative,

00:03:41.367 --> 00:03:45.100
something else you can do.
You can become an equestrian

00:03:45.100 --> 00:03:47.467
and learn how to take --
and ride horses,"

00:03:47.467 --> 00:03:50.400
and it changed
a lot of people's lives.

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:52.501
-For real. Honestly.

00:03:52.501 --> 00:03:54.334
It was a life-changing
experience

00:03:54.334 --> 00:03:55.767
working in Philadelphia.

00:03:55.767 --> 00:03:59.334
-Yeah. I mean, at the end of
the film -- well, no spoilers.

00:03:59.334 --> 00:04:01.267
But, well, too late.
I did it already.

00:04:01.267 --> 00:04:02.434
[ Laughter ]

00:04:02.434 --> 00:04:04.100
-You did it already.
-I really did it already.

00:04:04.100 --> 00:04:06.968
At the end of the film,
you see some real riders

00:04:06.968 --> 00:04:10.334
and members of the club
and you go, "Wow, that is a --"

00:04:10.334 --> 00:04:13.267
And they talk about
their life experience,

00:04:13.267 --> 00:04:14.801
how it changed their life.

00:04:14.801 --> 00:04:17.767
And it brings a lot of attention
to this organization,

00:04:17.767 --> 00:04:21.434
and they're currently trying to
raise money for it as well.

00:04:21.434 --> 00:04:22.968
-Yes. Exactly. Yeah.

00:04:22.968 --> 00:04:25.334
They've been there
over 100 years.

00:04:25.334 --> 00:04:26.801
A lot of people don't know that.

00:04:26.801 --> 00:04:28.868
They think that it's just
a thing that just happened now,

00:04:28.868 --> 00:04:31.934
but this is a part of history,
American history.

00:04:31.934 --> 00:04:33.734
But if you want to
find out more,

00:04:33.734 --> 00:04:35.934
you can look it up online,
thepura.org,

00:04:35.934 --> 00:04:39.167
or learn about what's going on
at Fletcher Street right now.

00:04:39.167 --> 00:04:42.067
Like, everything that you see
in the movie was there.

00:04:42.067 --> 00:04:43.934
Like, all the scenery
and everything.

00:04:43.934 --> 00:04:45.734
It was beautiful.
-That's wild.

00:04:45.734 --> 00:04:47.133
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:04:47.133 --> 00:04:50.300
Here is Caleb McLaughlin and
Idris Elba in "Concrete Cowboy."

00:04:50.300 --> 00:04:51.434
Take a look at this.

00:04:51.434 --> 00:04:53.267
-I can't --
-You need to take this lead.

00:04:53.267 --> 00:04:55.100
Alright? Click it on his halter.

00:04:55.100 --> 00:04:57.501
Alright?
Let him know that you're there.

00:04:57.501 --> 00:04:59.567
Let him know
that you're running this show.

00:04:59.567 --> 00:05:02.434
You understand me, Cole?
Come on. You got this.

00:05:02.434 --> 00:05:07.067
♪♪

00:05:07.067 --> 00:05:08.434
-Hey. Hey, boy.

00:05:08.434 --> 00:05:09.567
[ Horse grunts ]

00:05:09.567 --> 00:05:11.901
Okay. It's me, boy.

00:05:11.901 --> 00:05:13.868
You good. Hey.

00:05:13.868 --> 00:05:16.367
♪♪

00:05:16.367 --> 00:05:18.667
[ Horse neighs ]
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa, relax.

00:05:18.667 --> 00:05:20.701
It's okay. Chill. Chill.

00:05:20.701 --> 00:05:21.901
It's okay.

00:05:21.901 --> 00:05:23.767
♪♪

00:05:23.767 --> 00:05:25.834
[ Horse neighs ]

00:05:25.834 --> 00:05:27.968
-Come on, man.
You got this. You got this.

00:05:27.968 --> 00:05:31.601
-Alright. Hey, it's me.

00:05:31.601 --> 00:05:34.334
It's me, boy.

00:05:34.334 --> 00:05:35.868
[ Horse neighs ]

00:05:35.868 --> 00:05:38.801
-Yeah!
Caleb McLaughlin, everybody!

